n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The Landlord has played a very low single card (♣4). As the peasant playing immediately after the Landlord, I should beat this play to prevent the Landlord from easily passing the turn or playing more low cards. I have a large hand (17 cards) and need to offload useless cards. I hold an isolated single ♠7, which beats the 4 comfortably. Playing the 7 is efficient: it gets rid of a low "trash" card, preserves my pairs (44, 66, QQ) and triplets (333, 888), and is low enough that my teammate can easily play over it if they are in a strong position. Playing a high card like an Ace or 2 now would be a waste of a control card and might block my teammate.\n\nReason: The ♠7 is the lowest single card I can play that beats the ♣4 without breaking my pairs or triplets. It forces the game forward and allows me to shed a low card.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠7"]}'}
